# Three-way admixture (ternary)

**What this is.** When the cohort's effective label space is
exactly three RF labels, every sample is one point in an
equilateral triangle — vertices are the three labels, distance
to a vertex is that label's proportion. Each point's color is
RGB-mixed from its three proportions, so dominant-X samples sit
near vertex X in vertex-X color.

**How to read this chart.** Tight clusters near a vertex are
"clean" populations; samples strung along an edge are 2-way
admixed; samples in the interior are 3-way admixed. A diffuse
cloud (no clusters) is a sign that either the run is genuinely
heterogeneous or the label mapping is noisy.

